#: ../../../userguide/interfaces.rst:2
msgid "Supported Interfaces"
msgstr "支援的介面"

#: ../../../userguide/interfaces.rst:4
msgid ""
"Setuptools is a complicated library with many interface surfaces and "
"challenges. In addition to its primary purpose as a packaging build backend, "
"Setuptools also has historically served as a standalone builder, installer, "
"uploader, metadata provider, and more. Additionally, because it's "
"implemented as a Python library, its entire functionality is incidentally "
"exposed as a library."
msgstr ""
"Setuptools 是一個複雜的程式庫，擁有許多介面面和挑戰。除了作為打包建置後端的主"
"要用途外，Setuptools 在歷史上也擔任過獨立的建置工具、安裝工具、上傳工具、中繼"
"資料提供者等角色。此外，由於它以 Python 程式庫的形式實作，其全部功能也間接地"
"以程式庫的形式暴露出來。"

#: ../../../userguide/interfaces.rst:6
msgid ""
"In addition to operating as a library, because newer versions of Setuptools "
"are often used to build older (sometimes decades-old) packages, it has a "
"high burden of stability."
msgstr ""
"除了作為程式庫運作之外，由於新版本的 Setuptools 常被用來建置較舊的（有時是數"
"十年前的）軟體包，因此它承擔著很高的穩定性負擔。"

#: ../../../userguide/interfaces.rst:8
msgid ""
"In order to have the ability to make sensible changes to the project, "
"downstream developers and consumers should avoid depending on internal "
"implementation details of the library and should rely only on the supported "
"interfaces:"
msgstr ""
"為了能夠對專案進行合理的變更，下游開發者和使用者應避免依賴程式庫的內部實作細"
"節，而應僅依賴受支援的介面："

#: ../../../userguide/interfaces.rst:10
msgid ""
"*Tier 1*: APIs required by modern PyPA packaging standards (:pep:`517`, :pep:"
"`660`) and Documented APIs for customising build behavior or creating "
"plugins (:doc:`/userguide/extension`, :doc:`/references/keywords`):"
msgstr ""
"*第一層*：現代 PyPA 打包標準 (:pep:`517`, :pep:`660`) 所需的 API，以及用於自"
"訂建置行為或建立外掛程式的已文件化 API（:doc:`/userguide/extension`、:doc:`/"
"references/keywords`）："

#: ../../../userguide/interfaces.rst:12
msgid ""
"These APIs are expected to be extremely stable and have deprecation notices "
"and periods prior to backward incompatible changes or removals."
msgstr ""
"這些 API 預期將極為穩定，並且在向後不相容的變更或移除之前，會有棄用通知和緩衝"
"期。"

#: ../../../userguide/interfaces.rst:14
msgid ""
"Please note that *functional and integration tests* capture specific "
"behaviors and expectations about how the library and system is intended to "
"work for outside users; and *code comments and docstrings* (including in "
"tests) may provide specific protections to limit the changes to behaviors on "
"which a downstream consumer can rely."
msgstr ""
"請注意，*功能測試和整合測試* 捕捉了程式庫和系統預期如何為外部使用者運作的特定"
"行為和期望；而*程式碼註解和文件字串*（包括測試中的）可能提供特定保護，以限制"
"下游使用者可依賴的行為變更。"

#: ../../../userguide/interfaces.rst:17
msgid "*Tier 2*: Documented ``distutils`` APIs:"
msgstr "*第二層*：已文件化的 ``distutils`` API："

#: ../../../userguide/interfaces.rst:19
msgid ""
"``setuptools`` strives to honor the interfaces provided by ``distutils`` and "
"will coordinate with the ``pypa/distutils`` repository so that the "
"appropriate deprecation notices are issued."
msgstr ""
"``setuptools`` 致力於尊重 ``distutils`` 所提供的介面，並將與 ``pypa/"
"distutils`` 倉儲協調，以便發出適當的棄用通知。"

#: ../../../userguide/interfaces.rst:23
msgid ""
"In principle, these are documented in :doc:`/deprecated/distutils/apiref`. "
"Please note however that when a suitable replacement is available or "
"advised, the existing ``distutils`` API is considered deprecated and should "
"not be used (see :pep:`632#migration-advice` and :doc:`/deprecated/distutils-"
"legacy`)."
msgstr ""
"原則上，這些在 :doc:`/deprecated/distutils/apiref` 中有文件說明。但請注意，當"
"有合適的替代方案可用或建議使用時，現有的 ``distutils`` API 將被視為已棄用，不"
"應再使用（請參見 :pep:`632#migration-advice` 和 :doc:`/deprecated/distutils-"
"legacy`）。"

#: ../../../userguide/interfaces.rst:28
msgid ""
"Depending on other behaviors is risky and subject to future breakage. If a "
"project wishes to consider using interfaces that aren't covered above, "
"consider requesting those interfaces to be added prior to depending on them "
"(perhaps through a pull request implementing the change and relevant "
"regression tests)."
msgstr ""
"依賴其他行為是有風險的，且可能在未來遭受破壞。如果某個專案希望考慮使用上述未"
"涵蓋的介面，請考慮在依賴它們之前，先請求將這些介面加入（例如透過提交實作該變"
"更及相關回歸測試的拉取請求）。"

#: ../../../userguide/interfaces.rst:30
msgid ""
"Please check further information about deprecated and unsupported behaviors "
"in :doc:`/deprecated/index`."
msgstr ""
"請查閱\\ :doc:`/deprecated/index`\\ 以了解更多關於已棄用和不受支援行為的資"
"訊。"

#: ../../../userguide/interfaces.rst:34
msgid "Support Policy Exceptions"
msgstr "支援政策例外情況"

#: ../../../userguide/interfaces.rst:36
msgid ""
"Behaviors and interfaces explicitly documented/advertised as deprecated, or "
"that :obj:`issue deprecation warnings <warnings.warn>` will be supported up "
"to the end of the announced deprecation period."
msgstr ""
"明確記錄或宣告為已棄用的行為和介面，或發出\\ :obj:`棄用警告 <warnings."
"warn>`\\ 的項目，將在公告的棄用期限內繼續獲得支援。"

#: ../../../userguide/interfaces.rst:40
msgid ""
"However there are a few circumstances in which the Setuptools' maintainers "
"reserve the right of speeding up the deprecation cycle and shortening "
"deprecation periods:"
msgstr ""
"然而，在某些情況下，Setuptools 維護者保留加快棄用週期和縮短棄用期限的權利："

#: ../../../userguide/interfaces.rst:43
msgid ""
"When security vulnerabilities are identified in specific code paths and the "
"reworking existing APIs is not viable."
msgstr "當特定程式碼路徑中發現安全漏洞，且重新設計現有 API 不可行時。"

#: ../../../userguide/interfaces.rst:45
msgid ""
"When standards in the Python packaging ecosystem externally drive non-"
"backward compatible changes in the code base."
msgstr "當 Python 打包生態系統中的標準從外部驅動程式碼庫中的非向後相容變更時。"

#: ../../../userguide/interfaces.rst:47
msgid ""
"When changes in behavior are externally driven by 3rd-party dependencies and "
"code maintained outside of the ``pypa/setuptools`` repository."
msgstr ""
"當行為變更由第三方依賴以及在 ``pypa/setuptools`` 倉儲之外維護的程式碼外部驅動"
"時。"

#: ../../../userguide/interfaces.rst:50
msgid ""
"Note that these are exceptional circumstances and that the project will "
"carefully attempt to find alternatives before resorting to unscheduled "
"removals."
msgstr ""
"請注意，這些是例外情況，專案在訴諸於非預定移除之前，將仔細嘗試尋找替代方案。"

#: ../../../userguide/interfaces.rst:54
msgid ""
"In the context of ``setuptools``, the introduction of :py:mod:`warnings` "
"(including deprecation warnings) is not considered a breaking change *per "
"se*. Instead it is considered a backwards compatible *communication action* "
"that precedes an upcoming breaking change. This is becauset code containing "
"warnings typically does not fail and can successfully terminate execution, "
"unless users explicitly opt into transforming those warnings into errors (e."
"g., via Python's :external+python:ref:`-W option or PYTHONWARNINGS "
"environment variable <using-on-warnings>`)."
msgstr ""
"在 ``setuptools`` 的上下文中，引入 :py:mod:`warnings`（包括棄用警告）本身 *並"
"不* 被視為重大變更。相反地，它被視為一種向後相容的*溝通行為*，預示著即將到來"
"的重大變更。這是因為包含警告的程式碼通常不會失敗，並且可以成功完成執行，除非"
"使用者明確選擇將這些警告轉換為錯誤（例如，透過 Python 的 :external+python:"
"ref:`-W 選項或 PYTHONWARNINGS 環境變數 <using-on-warnings>`）。"

#: ../../../userguide/interfaces.rst:65
msgid "What to do when deprecation periods are undefined?"
msgstr "當棄用期限未定義時該怎麼辦？"

#: ../../../userguide/interfaces.rst:67
msgid ""
"In some cases it is difficult to define how long Setuptools will take to "
"remove certain features, behaviors or APIs. For example, it may be "
"complicated to assess how wide-spread the usage of a certain feature is in "
"the ecosystem."
msgstr ""
"在某些情況下，很難界定 Setuptools 需要多長時間來移除某些功能、行為或 API。例"
"如，評估某個功能在生態系統中的使用廣泛程度可能相當複雜。"

#: ../../../userguide/interfaces.rst:72
msgid ""
"Therefore, Setuptools may start to issue deprecation warnings without a "
"clear due date. This occurs because we want to notify consumers about "
"upcoming breaking changes as soon as possible so that they can start working "
"in migration plans."
msgstr ""
"因此，Setuptools 可能會在沒有明確到期日的情況下開始發出棄用警告。這是因為我們"
"希望盡快通知使用者即將到來的重大變更，以便他們可以開始制定遷移計畫。"

#: ../../../userguide/interfaces.rst:76
msgid ""
"This does not mean that users should treat this deprecation as low priority "
"or interpret the lack of due date as a signal that a breaking change will "
"never happen."
msgstr ""
"這並不意味著使用者應將此棄用視為低優先級，或將缺乏到期日解讀為重大變更永遠不"
"會發生的信號。"

#: ../../../userguide/interfaces.rst:79
msgid ""
"The advised course of action is for users to create a migration plan as soon "
"as they have identified to be subject to a Setuptools deprecation."
msgstr ""
"建議的做法是，使用者一旦發現自己受到 Setuptools 棄用影響，就應盡快制定遷移計"
"畫。"

#: ../../../userguide/interfaces.rst:82
msgid ""
"Setuptools may introduce relatively short deprecation periods (e.g. 6 "
"months) when a deprecation warning has already been issued for a long period "
"without a explicit due date."
msgstr ""
"當棄用警告已經在沒有明確到期日的情況下發出很長一段時間時，Setuptools 可能會引"
"入相對較短的棄用期限（例如 6 個月）。"

#: ../../../userguide/interfaces.rst:88
msgid "How to stay on top of upcoming deprecations?"
msgstr "如何掌握即將到來的棄用資訊？"

#: ../../../userguide/interfaces.rst:90
msgid ""
"It is a good idea to employ an automated test suite with relatively good "
"coverage in your project and keep an eye on the logs. You can also automate "
"this process by forwarding the standard output/error streams to a log file "
"and using heuristics to identify deprecations (e.g. by searching for the "
"word ``deprecation`` or ``deprecated``). You may need to increase the level "
"of verbosity of your output as some tools may hide log messages by default "
"(e.g. via ``pip -vv install ...``)."
msgstr ""
"最好在專案中使用覆蓋率較佳的自動化測試軟體包，並留意日誌。你也可以透過將標準"
"輸出/錯誤串流轉發到日誌檔案，並使用啟發式方法來識別棄用（例如搜尋 "
"``deprecation`` 或 ``deprecated`` 字詞）來自動化此過程。你可能需要提高輸出的"
"詳細程度，因為某些工具預設會隱藏日誌訊息（例如透過 ``pip -vv install ..."
"``）。"

#: ../../../userguide/interfaces.rst:98
msgid ""
"Additionally, if you are supporting a project that depends on Setuptools, "
"you can implement a CI workflow that leverages :external+python:ref:`Python "
"warning filters <warning-filter>` to improve the visibility of warnings."
msgstr ""
"此外，如果你維護的專案依賴於 Setuptools，你可以實作一個 CI 工作流程，利用 :"
"external+python:ref:`Python 警告過濾器 <warning-filter>` 來提高警告的可見度。"

#: ../../../userguide/interfaces.rst:103
msgid ""
"This workflow can be comprised, for example, of 3 iterative steps that "
"require developers to acknowledge the deprecation warnings:"
msgstr "此工作流程例如可以包含 3 個疊代步驟，要求開發者確認棄用警告："

#: ../../../userguide/interfaces.rst:106
msgid ""
"Leverage Python Warning's Filter to transform warnings into exceptions "
"during automated tests."
msgstr "利用 Python 警告過濾器，在自動化測試期間將警告轉換為例外。"

#: ../../../userguide/interfaces.rst:107
msgid "Devise a migration plan:"
msgstr "制定遷移計畫："

#: ../../../userguide/interfaces.rst:109
msgid ""
"It is a good idea to track deprecations as if they were issues, and apply "
"project management techniques to monitor the progress in handling them."
msgstr "最好將棄用事項像問題一樣追蹤，並應用專案管理技術來監控處理進度。"

#: ../../../userguide/interfaces.rst:111
msgid ""
"Determine which parts of your code are affected and understand the changes "
"required to eliminate the warnings."
msgstr "判斷程式碼中哪些部分受到影響，並了解消除警告所需的變更。"

#: ../../../userguide/interfaces.rst:114
msgid ""
"Modify the warning's filter you are using in the CI to not fail with the "
"newly identified exceptions (e.g. by using the ``default`` action with a "
"specific category or regular expression for the warning message). This can "
"be done globally for the whole test suite or locally in a test-by-test basis."
msgstr ""
"修改你在 CI 中使用的警告過濾器，使其不會因為新識別的例外而失敗（例如，使用 "
"``default`` 動作搭配特定的類別或正規表達式來比對警告訊息）。這可以針對整個測"
"試軟體包全域設定，也可以在逐項測試的基礎上局部設定。"

#: ../../../userguide/interfaces.rst:120
msgid ""
"Test tools like :pypi:`pytest` offer CLI and configuration options to "
"facilitate controlling the warning's filter (see :external+pytest:doc:`how-"
"to/capture-warnings`)."
msgstr ""
"像 :pypi:`pytest` 這樣的測試工具提供了 CLI 和設定選項，以便於控制警告過濾器"
"（請參見 :external+pytest:doc:`how-to/capture-warnings`）。"

#: ../../../userguide/interfaces.rst:123
msgid ""
"Note that there are many ways to incorporate such workflow in your CI. For "
"example, if you have enough deployment resources and consider deprecation "
"warning management to be a day-to-day development test you can set the "
"warning's filter directly on your main CI loop. On the other hand if you "
"have critical timelines and cannot afford CI jobs occasionally failing to "
"flag maintenance, you can consider scheduling a periodic CI run separated "
"from your main/mission-critical workflow."
msgstr ""
"請注意，有許多方式可以將此工作流程整合到你的 CI 中。例如，如果你有足夠的部署"
"資源，並將棄用警告管理視為日常開發測試，你可以直接在主要 CI 迴圈中設定警告過"
"濾器。另一方面，如果你有嚴格的時間表，無法承受 CI 工作偶爾因標記維護而失敗，"
"你可以考慮排程一個與主要/關鍵任務工作流程分開的定期 CI 執行。"

#: ../../../userguide/interfaces.rst:133
msgid "What does \"support\" mean?"
msgstr "「支援」是什麼意思？"

#: ../../../userguide/interfaces.rst:135
msgid ""
"Setuptools is a non-profit community-driven open source project and as such "
"the word \"support\" is used in a best-effort manner and with limited scope. "
"For example, it is not always possible to quickly provide fixes for bugs."
msgstr ""
"Setuptools 是一個非營利、由社群驅動的開源專案，因此「支援」一詞是以盡力而為且"
"範圍有限的方式使用。例如，並非總能快速提供錯誤修正。"

#: ../../../userguide/interfaces.rst:139
msgid ""
"We appreciate the patience of the community and incentivise users impacted "
"by bugs to contribute to fixes in the form of :doc:`PR submissions </"
"development/developer-guide>`, to speed-up the process."
msgstr ""
"我們感謝社群的耐心，並鼓勵受到錯誤影響的使用者以\\ :doc:`提交 PR </"
"development/developer-guide>` 的形式貢獻修正，以加快處理速度。"

#: ../../../userguide/interfaces.rst:143
msgid ""
"When we say \"a certain feature is supported\" we mean that we will do our "
"best to ensure this feature keeps working as documented. Note however that, "
"as in any system, unintended breakages may happen. We appreciate the "
"community understand and `considerate feedback`_."
msgstr ""
"當我們說「某個功能受到支援」時，意思是我們會盡最大努力確保該功能按文件說明的"
"正常運作。但請注意，與任何系統一樣，仍可能發生非預期的損壞。我們感謝社群的理"
"解與\\ `體貼的回饋 <considerate feedback>`_\\ 。"

#: ../../../userguide/interfaces.rst:152
msgid "What to do after the deprecation period ends?"
msgstr "棄用期限結束後該怎麼辦？"

#: ../../../userguide/interfaces.rst:154
msgid ""
"If you have limited development resources and is not able to devise a "
"migration plan before Setuptools removes a deprecated feature, you can still "
"resort to restricting the version of Setuptools to be installed. This "
"usually includes modifying ``[build-system] requires`` in ``pyproject.toml`` "
"and/or specifying ``pip`` :external+pip:ref:`Constraints Files` via the "
"``PIP_CONSTRAINT`` environment variable (or passing |build-constraint-uv|_). "
"Please avoid however to preemptively add version constraints if not "
"necessary, (you can read more about this in https://iscinumpy.dev/post/bound-"
"version-constraints/)."
msgstr ""
"如果你的開發資源有限，無法在 Setuptools 移除已棄用功能之前制定遷移計畫，你仍"
"然可以限制所安裝的 Setuptools 版本。這通常包括修改 ``pyproject.toml`` 中的 "
"``[build-system] requires``，和/或透過 ``PIP_CONSTRAINT`` 環境變數指定 "
"``pip`` :external+pip:ref:`約束檔案 <Constraints Files>`（或傳遞 |build-"
"constraint-uv|_）。但請避免在沒有必要的情況下預先加入版本約束（你可以在 "
"https://iscinumpy.dev/post/bound-version-constraints/ 閱讀更多相關資訊）。"

#: ../../../userguide/interfaces.rst:168
msgid "A note on \"Public Names\""
msgstr "關於「公開名稱」的說明"

#: ../../../userguide/interfaces.rst:170
msgid ""
"Python devs may be used to the convention that private members are prefixed "
"with an ``_`` (underscore) character and that any member not marked by this "
"public. Due to the history and legacy of Setuptools this is not necessarily "
"the case [#private]_."
msgstr ""
"Python 開發者可能習慣於私有成員以 ``_``（底線）字元為前綴的慣例，並且任何未被"
"此標記的成員即為公開。但由於 Setuptools 的歷史和遺留問題，情況並非一定如此 "
"[#private]_。"

#: ../../../userguide/interfaces.rst:175
msgid ""
"In this project, \"public interfaces\" are defined as interfaces explicitly "
"documented for 3rd party consumption."
msgstr "在此專案中，「公開介面」被定義為明確文件化供第三方使用的介面。"

#: ../../../userguide/interfaces.rst:178
msgid ""
"When accessing a member in the ``setuptools`` package, please make sure it "
"is documented for external usage. Also note that names imported from "
"different modules/submodules are considered internal implementation details "
"unless explicitly listed in ``__all__``. The fact that they are accessible "
"in the namespace of the ``import``-er module is a mere side effect of the "
"way Python works."
msgstr ""
"在存取 ``setuptools`` 軟體包中的成員時，請確保該成員已被文件化為外部用途。另"
"請注意，從不同模組/子模組匯入的名稱被視為內部實作細節，除非它們被明確列在 "
"``__all__`` 中。它們在執行 ``import`` 的模組命名空間中可被存取，這只是 "
"Python 運作方式的副作用。"

#: ../../../userguide/interfaces.rst:185
msgid ""
"While names prefixed by ``_`` are always considered private, not necessary "
"the absence of the prefix signals public members."
msgstr ""
"雖然以 ``_`` 為前綴的名稱始終被視為私有，但沒有此前綴並不一定表示該成員為公"
"開。"
